[ system ]
{# Sent by SN_SexualHistory.dll when an OStim or SexLab scene ends, once for everyone who took part, the player included.
   The answer becomes that participant's SkyrimNet memory of the scene.
   Context: owner_name, owner_form_id, framework, location, game_date, real_minutes,
   participants (list of {name, form_id, is_player, is_owner, memories}), scene_details (list),
   climaxes (list of names), events (list of "Name -> Target (type): text", oldest first). #}
You are an expert on the Elder Scrolls universe, especially Skyrim. Your task is to turn an intimate encounter into a coherent first-person memory for a character within the game.

{{ render_template("submodules\\system_head\\0010_setting") }}

Generate a first-person memory for {{ owner_name }} of the intimate encounter described below.

## You
{{ render_character_profile("full", formid_to_uuid(owner_form_id)) }}

## Instructions
Write the memory from {{ owner_name }}'s perspective:
1. Write in first person, as a recollection (no "last week" etc.).
2. Say who took part, where, and what happened between them, using their names.
3. Say how {{ owner_name }} felt during and after it, and how the others seemed to feel, judging from what they said and did and from the memories listed for them. Stay true to {{ owner_name }}'s personality and to how they already feel about the others.
4. Mention what was said or done around the encounter when it matters (how it began, promises, quarrels, what came after).
5. Use only what is given. Do not invent events, lines or relationships.
6. Be frank but not graphic: name what happened plainly, without lurid detail.
7. 3-6 dense sentences. Use concrete, searchable terms (names, places, actions).
8. Write in the same language as the character profile and the events.

## Response Format
Respond ONLY with a JSON object:
{% raw %}
```json
{
  "content": "First-person memory, 3-6 sentences: who, where, what happened, how I and the others felt.",
  "emotion": "joyful|content|neutral|concerned|fearful|angry|disgusted|surprised|sad|traumatized",
  "importance_score": 0.0-1.0,
  "tags": ["name", "location", "action", "theme"],
  "type": "RELATIONSHIP|JOY|TRAUMA|EXPERIENCE"
}
```
{% endraw %}

- type: RELATIONSHIP when it changed or confirmed a bond, JOY when it was mainly a happy experience, TRAUMA when it was forced or distressing for {{ owner_name }}, EXPERIENCE otherwise.
- importance_score: 0.7-1.0 for a first time, a forced encounter, or one that changes a relationship; 0.4-0.6 for one between established partners; lower only for something {{ owner_name }} cares little about.
- tags: 5-10 lower-case tags (names, place, acts, themes).

[ user ]
Memory owner: {{ owner_name }}
Location: {{ location }}
In-game time: {{ game_date }}
Duration (real time): about {{ real_minutes }} minutes

Participants:
{% for p in participants %}- {{ p.name }}{% if p.is_owner %} (THIS IS YOU){% endif %}{% if p.is_player %} (the player){% endif %}: {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", formid_to_uuid(p.form_id)) }}
{% if length(p.memories) > 0 %}    Relevant memories of {{ p.name }}:
{% for m in p.memories %}    - {{ m }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
What the scene showed ({{ framework }}), in order:
{% if length(scene_details) == 0 %}- (no details recorded)
{% else %}{% for d in scene_details %}- {{ d }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if length(climaxes) > 0 %}Climaxes: {% for c in climaxes %}{{ c }}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
Events recorded during the scene (oldest first):
{% if length(events) == 0 %}- (none)
{% else %}{% for e in events %}- {{ e }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
